      "priority": "MEDIUM",
      "category": "Policy",
      "description": "Recommendation 1: Limit CPT 59510 and 59430 to the same pregnancy and the same TIN or same provider/group TIN, with 59510 payable once per pregnancy and only one postpartum period per pregnancy / 90-day postpartum period; bundle or deny duplicate claim history for repeat 59510 or 59430. Exempt: assistant surgeon cesarean deliveries, not global package postpartum care. Peer: Point32Health allows one global package per pregnancy, United Health allows one delivery code per birth episode and one postpartum package per delivery, and Highmark_BCBS allows one antepartum/postpartum period per delivery episode..\n\nRecommendation 2: Allow separate assistant-surgeon reimbursement for cesarean delivery codes 59510, 59514, 59515, 59618, 59620, and 59622 only when modifier 80, 81, 82, or AS is present; otherwise bundle the assistant-surgeon line into the maternity package. Exempt: assistant surgeon cesarean deliveries, assistant surgeon on cesarean delivery with appropriate modifier. Peer: Cigna and Point32Health require modifier 80, 81, 82, or AS for assistant surgeon billing on cesarean delivery codes, while United Health separately recognizes assistant surgeon billed scenarios..",
